(217024, 12167, 3585, '<td valign="top">Congratulations Mirko on this great photograph</td>', 'Congratulations Mirko on this great photograph', '2003-02-17 03:12:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(217042, 12142, 2217, '<td valign="top">The first thing that sprung to mind when I saw the Waldo challenge was of a painted person in front of a similarly painted background.  I painted my son white which was the undercoat for all the designs.  I took a few silly pictures while he was still white and started painting the final designs on him. I never liked any of the final pictures with all the designs and started fooling around with one of the white ones.  The original wasn''t striking in anyway, quite awful in fact.  I played with levels, curves and saturation in photoshop 7 and was quite surprised how it came out.  I liked it and since I never came up with anything else that week I entered it thinking that either it would be well received or a dismal failure.</td>', 'The first thing that sprung to mind when I saw the Waldo challenge was of a painted person in front of a similarly painted background.  I painted my son white which was the undercoat for all the designs.  I took a few silly pictures while he was still white and started painting the final designs on him. I never liked any of the final pictures with all the designs and started fooling around with one of the white ones.  The original wasn''t striking in anyway, quite awful in fact.  I played with levels, curves and saturation in photoshop 7 and was quite surprised how it came out.  I liked it and since I never came up with anything else that week I entered it thinking that either it would be well received or a dismal failure.', '2003-02-17 03:21:39.000000', NULL, 0),
(217084, 12284, 3540, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club<br/>By Inspzil<br/> <br/>Composition - Awesome background.  The snowy trees are great.  I''m not so sure about the foreground part.  I think you may have had a little more success with this shot if you didn''t take it so close.  I think you''d have been better served it the photo was from 20 feet or so.  I do think you met the challenge.<br/> <br/>Technical - Snow exposures are always tough.  I think you did fairly well with this one.  Honestly I think I probably wouldn''t have done much better, if at all.  Dark trees + snow=something is over or under exposed.  Focus might be a little sharper but not bad.  I think putting this in black and white might''ve helped a little.  This is not an easy photo to take and with the substantial contrast, hard to even process into a good photo.<br/> <br/>Overall - I think you did well with your estimate.  It wasn''t posted to win any awards and I''m glad you realize that.  The composition is cute, but not anything to write home about.  The photography isn''t bad, but for the conditions, you did pretty well.  Sorry this can''t be more helpful for you.  All things considered on this end, I''m doing ok for 5:00am by writing this!  Good luck in the upcoming challenges - Inspzil</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique ClubBy Inspzil Composition - Awesome background.  The snowy trees are great.  I''m not so sure about the foreground part.  I think you may have had a little more success with this shot if you didn''t take it so close.  I think you''d have been better served it the photo was from 20 feet or so.  I do think you met the challenge. Technical - Snow exposures are always tough.  I think you did fairly well with this one.  Honestly I think I probably wouldn''t have done much better, if at all.  Dark trees + snow=something is over or under exposed.  Focus might be a little sharper but not bad.  I think putting this in black and white might''ve helped a little.  This is not an easy photo to take and with the substantial contrast, hard to even process into a good photo. Overall - I think you did well with your estimate.  It wasn''t posted to win any awards and I''m glad you realize that.  The composition is cute, but not anything to write home about.  The photography isn''t bad, but for the conditions, you did pretty well.  Sorry this can''t be more helpful for you.  All things considered on this end, I''m doing ok for 5:00am by writing this!  Good luck in the upcoming challenges - Inspzil', '2003-02-17 04:56:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(217097, 12167, 6418, '<td valign="top">Congratulations!!  I knew it!!!!  Really beautiful shot, and I will print this out and put it on the wall in my bed room!!  Great job!!</td>', 'Congratulations!!  I knew it!!!!  Really beautiful shot, and I will print this out and put it on the wall in my bed room!!  Great job!!', '2003-02-17 05:38:14.000000', NULL, 0),
(217101, 12279, 6418, '<td valign="top">""Very patient set up. The real waldo, too! Middle plane of focus may get you some focus comments. Did you do this for a reason (maybe to help "hide" your Waldo?)? But your background is so plain, Waldo still stands out plainly. Maybe more coins??? 7 Swash""<br/> <br/>Thank you Swash, and your comment explained everything I needed to say on my picture.  It was a confusing challenge for me. Just wanted to say that I can''t see on the rule saying "You are supposed to put a "REAL PERSON" anywhere!  In my language, person could mean anything including in the cartoon world or even animals for some occasions. The challenge title was "Where''s Waldo?" Right? Also, I made Waldo out of focus to hide him in the picture, so that he is meant be out of focus...  I leant a lot from this challenge, and I will try more simple, and undarstandable shots from now on!!  lol!!<br/> <br/>Well, I think I still like this one, and the cropping I did was a bit wrong and more coins definitely would have made it better...  Well, I really enjoyed taking this picture!  Yes, was quite annoying to stand the coins up... They kept fallen down, and made me crazy!!  <br/> <br/>Anyway, I don''t want to be rude, just needed to defend myself a bit this time...  Thank you all for all the votes and comments, and let''s have fun on next challenge!!</td>', '""Very patient set up. The real waldo, too! Middle plane of focus may get you some focus comments. Did you do this for a reason (maybe to help "hide" your Waldo?)? But your background is so plain, Waldo still stands out plainly. Maybe more coins??? 7 Swash"" Thank you Swash, and your comment explained everything I needed to say on my picture.  It was a confusing challenge for me. Just wanted to say that I can''t see on the rule saying "You are supposed to put a "REAL PERSON" anywhere!  In my language, person could mean anything including in the cartoon world or even animals for some occasions. The challenge title was "Where''s Waldo?" Right? Also, I made Waldo out of focus to hide him in the picture, so that he is meant be out of focus...  I leant a lot from this challenge, and I will try more simple, and undarstandable shots from now on!!  lol!! Well, I think I still like this one, and the cropping I did was a bit wrong and more coins definitely would have made it better...  Well, I really enjoyed taking this picture!  Yes, was quite annoying to stand the coins up... They kept fallen down, and made me crazy!!   Anyway, I don''t want to be rude, just needed to defend myself a bit this time...  Thank you all for all the votes and comments, and let''s have fun on next challenge!!', '2003-02-17 05:54:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(217135, 12167, 6815, '<td valign="top">Praza Stross i cura koja se skrila iza svjetiljke. Jako lijepo si ovo napravio.</td>', 'Praza Stross i cura koja se skrila iza svjetiljke. Jako lijepo si ovo napravio.', '2003-02-17 07:49:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(217200, 12107, 5521, '<td valign="top">Thank you everybody for your votes and special thanks to all the people that left comments.<br/> <br/>The structure in the photo is the observation tower of the Lonsdale Quay Hotel in North Vancouver, BC. This scene is one that I have enjoyed many times when walking back home after work. The tower is accessible to the public and it is not uncommon to find a photographer on it since this is one of the best spots to photograph the northern skyline of downtown Vancouver. This photo was taking facing west. Vancouvers harbour and downtown are south of were the camera was standing.<br/> <br/>The photo is not posed, so I took many shots waiting on each of them for the rotating sign to face my way. The photographer is hidden in some of the shots but because he is a silhouette, it is impossible to recognize him as a person. It all went down to a choice between showing an easy and an impossible to see person.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-02-17 09:36:01.</i></td>', 'Thank you everybody for your votes and special thanks to all the people that left comments. The structure in the photo is the observation tower of the Lonsdale Quay Hotel in North Vancouver, BC. This scene is one that I have enjoyed many times when walking back home after work. The tower is accessible to the public and it is not uncommon to find a photographer on it since this is one of the best spots to photograph the northern skyline of downtown Vancouver. This photo was taking facing west. Vancouvers harbour and downtown are south of were the camera was standing. The photo is not posed, so I took many shots waiting on each of them for the rotating sign to face my way. The photographer is hidden in some of the shots but because he is a silhouette, it is impossible to recognize him as a person. It all went down to a choice between showing an easy and an impossible to see person.', '2003-02-17 09:35:44.000000', '2003-02-17 09:36:01.000000', 0),
(217211, 12167, 806, '<td valign="top">Congrats.. You know.. I couldn''t find Waldo, but I like the shot..<br/>...and I love your description in the details (lol) nice verbal map!</td>', 'Congrats.. You know.. I couldn''t find Waldo, but I like the shot.....and I love your description in the details (lol) nice verbal map!', '2003-02-17 09:46:19.000000', NULL, 0),
(217212, 12175, 806, '<td valign="top">Love the image, love the title!</td>', 'Love the image, love the title!', '2003-02-17 09:47:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(217215, 12297, 1808, '<td valign="top">OK, OK, there was not actually a human being in the picture, but if you look at the "negative space" between the trees, it sure looks like a person to me, particularly the legs on the bottom half.<br/></td>', 'OK, OK, there was not actually a human being in the picture, but if you look at the "negative space" between the trees, it sure looks like a person to me, particularly the legs on the bottom half.', '2003-02-17 09:52:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(217247, 12122, 715, '<td valign="top">Thanks a lot for the comments and votes.<br/> <br/>The description of this photo tells how it''s done. Just want to add to that, that I used a 500 Watt worklight on a stand at about 4 ft distance.<br/>I did try some shots whith a more soft lighting and with the light at a longer distance, but it made the image look flat and less dramatic.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks a lot for the comments and votes. The description of this photo tells how it''s done. Just want to add to that, that I used a 500 Watt worklight on a stand at about 4 ft distance.I did try some shots whith a more soft lighting and with the light at a longer distance, but it made the image look flat and less dramatic. ', '2003-02-17 10:30:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(217254, 12142, 714, '<td valign="top">Jean,  this is an outstanding photo.  It is neat the way you come up with the final shot.  Congrats on 3rd place.</td>', 'Jean,  this is an outstanding photo.  It is neat the way you come up with the final shot.  Congrats on 3rd place.', '2003-02-17 10:32:52.000000', NULL, 0),
